{"path":"regex/match_results/operator=","title":"std::match_results<BidirIt,Alloc>::operator=","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::match_results&lt;BidirIt,Alloc&gt;::</span>operator=","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/regex/match_results/operator=","section":"regex","kind":"page","summary":"Given the value of other before the assignment as m and any integer in [ 0 , m.size()) as n, when the assignment finishes, the following member functions should return the specified values:","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/regex\">&lt;regex&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">match_results<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> operator<span class=\"sy1\">=</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> match_results<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> other <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">match_results<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> operator<span class=\"sy1\">=</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> match_results<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> other <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Assigns the contents.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Copy assignment operator. Assigns the contents of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code>. </div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Move assignment operator. Assigns the contents of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> using move semantics. <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> is in a valid, but unspecified state after the operation. </div>\n<p>Given the value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> before the assignment as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m</span></code> and any integer in <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code><code>)</code></span> as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">n</span></code>, when the assignment finishes, the following member functions should return the specified values:\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tr>\n<th>&nbsp;Member function&nbsp;\n</th>\n<th>Value\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/regex/match_results/ready\"><code>ready()</code></a>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m.<span class=\"me1\">ready</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/regex/match_results/size\"><code>size()</code></a>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/regex/match_results/str\"><code>str(n)</code></a>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m.<span class=\"me1\">str</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>n<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/regex/match_results/prefix\"><code>prefix()</code></a>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m.<span class=\"me1\">prefix</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/regex/match_results/suffix\"><code>suffix()</code></a>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m.<span class=\"me1\">suffix</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/regex/match_results/operator_at\"><code>operator[](n)</code></a>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m<span class=\"br0\">[</span>n<span class=\"br0\">]</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/regex/match_results/length\"><code>length(n)</code></a>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m.<span class=\"me1\">length</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>n<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/regex/match_results/position\"><code>position(n)</code></a>\n</td>\n<td>&nbsp;<code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m.<span class=\"me1\">position</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>n<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>&nbsp;\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> other\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> another match results object\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> May throw implementation-defined exceptions.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2191\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 2191</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++11\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">n</span></code> could be negative in the postconditions\n</td>\n<td>can only be non-negative\n</td></tr></table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"regex","title":"Regular expressions library (since C++11)"},{"path":"regex/match_results","title":"std::match_results"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::match_results<BidirIt,Alloc>::operator=","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. Assigns the contents."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"other"},{"label":"Return value","note":"*this"},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"May throw implementation-defined exceptions."}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":158,"codeBlockCount":0}
